# XCU dot
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The special built-in utilities are described inside
# utilities/V3_chap02.html (the page utilities/dot.html only redirects
# there), so anchors name V3_chap02.html and the .cov file accounts for
# the units by hand.

assertion  XCU.dot.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/execute the resulting commands in the current environment
class      required
says       The dot utility executes the commands of the file in the current
           shell environment: variables, functions and positional parameters
           it sets stay set.
test       t/001-current-env.sh

assertion  XCU.dot.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/need not be executable
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/search path specified by
class      required
says       A file operand without a slash is looked for in the directories
           of PATH and need not be executable; the current directory is not
           searched unless PATH names it.
test       t/002-path-search.sh

assertion  XCU.dot.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/does not contain a
class      required
says       A file operand that contains a slash is used as given, with no
           PATH search.
test       t/003-slash-name.sh

assertion  XCU.dot.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/return the value of the last command executed
class      required
says       The status of the dot utility is that of the last command
           executed in the file, and zero when the file runs no command.
test       t/004-status.sh

assertion  XCU.dot.005
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/If no readable file is found
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1
class      required
says       When no readable file is found, a non-interactive shell exits
           with a non-zero status and runs nothing more.
test       t/005-not-found.sh

assertion  XCU.dot.006
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/diagnostic message to standard error
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/the shell is interactive
class      required
says       When no readable file is found, an interactive shell writes a
           diagnostic to standard error, does not exit, and the dot utility
           returns a non-zero status.
test       t/006-not-found-interactive.sh

assertion  XCU.dot.007
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/parse the tokens
class      required
says       A syntax error in the file read by dot makes a non-interactive
           shell exit with a non-zero status; commands after the dot are not
           run.
test       t/007-syntax-error.sh

assertion  XCU.dot.008
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/special built-in shall support XBD
class      required
since      2024
says       The dot utility accepts "--" as the end of options before the
           file operand.
test       t/008-double-hyphen.sh
